<http://data.silknow.org/object/eab6b1de-c338-325d-bb97-5c1f4193146b/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "woven silk and metal thread with a border of woven silk and metal thread, backed with plain weave printed cotton and faced with woven silk.\nThe purple/aubergine ground is covered with metal thread [silver strip open S-wound on yellow and on white silk] with red silk highlights. The pattern is alternating rows of double flowers in silver thread [on a white core] and alternating 4-petalled flower heads in gold thread [yellow core] and silver thread [white core].\nBorder: pieced. Yellow silk ground woven with large and small scale botehs in pink, blue and green and metal thread.\nBacking: red cotton printed with a repeating zigzag of branches and daisies in light red. The backing is attached to the front by two rows of widely-spaced straight stitches.\nFacing: bias cut black silk."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/eab6b1de-c338-325d-bb97-5c1f4193146b> .

<http://data.silknow.org/event/cdf6b002-90b0-3d1c-94ff-d3226536f3f4>
