        rdfs:comment                   "woven silk and metal thread with a border of woven silk and metal thread, backed with plain weave printed cotton and faced with woven silk.\nThe purple/aubergine ground is covered with metal thread [silver strip open S-wound on yellow and on white silk] with red silk highlights. The pattern is alternating rows of double flowers in silver thread [on a white core] and alternating 4-petalled flower heads in gold thread [yellow core] and silver thread [white core].\nBorder: pieced. Yellow silk ground woven with large and small scale botehs in pink, blue and green and metal thread.\nBacking: red cotton printed with a repeating zigzag of branches and daisies in light red. The backing is attached to the front by two rows of widely-spaced straight stitches.\nFacing: bias cut black silk."@en , "Middle East, Textile;"@en ;
